From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?=
 <5814559+villekivela@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:59:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extensions: let an offscreen document select text

Selecting text in an offscreen document took the browser down. A
password manager copies a password from its offscreen document by
putting it in a text area, selecting it and calling
document.execCommand("copy"), so the first copy that reached that
document ended the session. The document's contents were created by the
extension system, so its RenderWidgetHostViewQt has no delegate, and the
text input state, selection and focused node changes the selection
reports each reached for it: OnUpdateTextInputStateCalled() dereferenced
the null delegate, and the selection handlers go on to the missing
adapter client.

Each of OnUpdateTextInputStateCalled(), OnSelectionBoundsChanged(),
OnTextSelectionChanged() and FocusedNodeChanged() now returns before it
reaches the delegate when there is none. Such a view has no input method
and no one to report a selection to. This follows 0019, which made
Hide() and IsShowing() handle the same missing delegate. Stock
QtWebEngine 6.11.2 crashes the same way.

anOffscreenDocumentCanSelectText selects text in an offscreen document,
removes the text area and waits for the reports to arrive. Without this
patch the test program dies with SIGSEGV in
RenderWidgetHostViewQt::OnUpdateTextInputStateCalled().

See villekivela/omaweb#745.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
